WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
At a party and need to learn Oops, All In right now?

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.100
Grab your own phone and type in

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.300
the four-letter room code on the website.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.300
Everyone starts with 100 pretend chips.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.500
Every round features a quick mini game.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.200
But before you actually play, you bet on yourself.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.400
When it is your turn, you can stay in to match,

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.400
raise or fold.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.800
Do not worry about losing everything right away.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.300
In rounds one and two, bets are capped at 20 chips.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.900
But starting in round three, the betting limits disappear.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.700
You can push every single chip you have and go Oops, All In.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.600
Some mini games use judges to pick the best answer.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:40.600
Judges just vote.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.300
They never bet on that round.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:45.400
Whoever has the most chips at the end of the game wins.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.600
Pro tip: start in Minigames mode

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.800
to learn without any chips first.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:52.400
Now grab your phone, type in that room code

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:53.400
and go take the pot.
